---
title: "Incident timeline: Thursday 26 February 2026, ~10 PM, to Friday ~10 PM"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant E as Engineer
    participant AI as AI agent
    participant TF as Terraform
    participant AWS as AWS (production)

    Note over E: Thursday ~10 PM, new computer, state on the old one
    E->>AI: Deploy the website changes with Terraform
    AI->>TF: terraform plan
    Note over TF: No state: plans to create everything again
    AI->>TF: terraform apply
    TF->>AWS: Starts creating duplicate resources
    E->>AI: Why are we creating so many resources?
    AI-->>E: Terraform believed nothing existed
    Note over E: Cancels the apply, copies the Terraform archive from the old computer
    E->>AI: Find and delete the duplicates
    AI->>AI: Unpacks the archive, replacing the state with production's
    AI-->>E: A terraform destroy would be cleaner
    AI->>TF: terraform destroy -auto-approve
    TF->>AWS: Deletes the VPC, RDS database, ECS cluster, load balancers, and bastion
    Note over AWS: Automated snapshots deleted too
    Note over E: Friday ~12 AM, support ticket and Business Support upgrade
    AWS-->>E: A snapshot exists on AWS's side
    Note over E: Friday ~10 PM, about 24 hours after the deletion
    AWS-->>E: Snapshot restored: 1,943,200 rows in courses_answer
